
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3002/api
@contentType = application/json


### 1. Register
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "lastName": "Martin",
  "firstName": "Thomas",
  "email": "thomas.martin@email.fr",
  "password": "Password123@",
  "address": "45 avenue des Chênes",
  "postalCode": "69001",
  "city": "Lyon",
  "type": "particulier",
  "phone": "0612345678"
}


### 2. Login → stocke le token
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "thomas.martin@email.fr",
  "password": "Password123@"
}



###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}


### 3. GET /me — profil
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 4. PUT /me — mise à jour
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "city": "Lyon",
  "postalCode": "69000",
  "phone": "0612345678"
}


### 5. PUT /me — KO email invalide (400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{ "email": "pas-un-email" }


### 6. PUT /me — KO body vide (400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{}


### 7. GET /me — KO sans token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me


### 8. GET /me — KO token invalide (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer un.token.invalide


### 9. GET /me/orders — historique
# @name listOrders
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@orderId = {{listOrders.response.body.data[0].id}}


### 10. GET /me/orders/:id — détail
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 11. GET /me/orders/:id — KO id inexistant (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/orders/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 12. GET /me/orders/:id — KO id non numérique (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/orders/abc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 13. GET /me/orders — KO sans token (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me/orders


### 14. DELETE /me — suppression (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 15. GET /me — après suppression (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 16. POST /auth/logout — déconnexion (200)
### Stateless JWT : le serveur renvoie juste un message,
### c'est au frontend de jeter le token.
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
